  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Union Cabinet has moved to introduce a new delimitation bill, designated as the 132nd Constitutional Amendment, which aims to increase the total number of Lok Sabha seats to 650. The proposal includes a provision for one-third reservation for women in both Parliament and state assemblies, to be implemented via a rotational system. The initiative has sparked intense political debate across India. Proponents, including key regional allies of the ruling party, describe the move as a historic step toward empowering women and ensuring governance remains representative. Conversely, opposition parties have expressed significant concerns, suggesting the exercise may favor the ruling party politically while potentially undermining the interests of southern states. Critics are calling for a coordinated strategy to stall the bill, warning that the changes could weaken federal structures and impact the balance of power between different regions.",
